  "important_failures_retained": [
    "Parallel ring startup ENOMEM with default 8 MiB process memlock; scoped per-process increase passes all tests.",
    "Manual Mio poller fixtures retain the native driver; all 52 network integration tests explicitly select Monoio. The initial fixture-selection failure remains archived.",
    "Initial mixed acceptance saw one extra established socket. Retained readiness descriptor test reproduces a TCP lifetime gap. Explicit shutdown passes regression and two final mixed cases. This is an integration finding, not proof of a Monoio library bug."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "io_uring readiness and scheduler adaptation; existing borrowed read/sendmsg transport retained. Owned-buffer completion I/O, provided buffers and kernel zero-copy sends are unmeasured.",
    "Safe independent readiness ownership duplicates each socket to preserve direct cross-worker writing. This is an adapter choice, not an inherent Monoio requirement.",
    "Four server cores0-3. Private clients4-7 share server L3; capacity/fanout clients8-15 use the other L3. Compare within cohorts.",
    "Short loopback trials; no WAN/TLS or multi-hour claim. Server RSS excludes kernel and clients; the offered million messages/s overloads both four-worker servers."
  ],
